1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
A FUNCTIONAL LOCAL PROOF OF CONCEPT
Document questions. Finance calculations. HR policy checks. Access control. Database automation. This captioned visual walkthrough uses actual browser screenshots from the running local application. Local evidence mode is shown. The optional OpenAI integration was tested with HTTP mocks; no live model call was made. Generated with OpenAI Codex. Contribution details are in DISCLOSURE.md.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:20,000
01 / THE WORKSPACE
Six synthetic source documents, two specialist advisors, and role-aware access. No API key is needed for the local evidence demo.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:32,000
02 / FINANCIAL ACCURACY
Q3 gross margin is recomputed in Python: (1,200,000 - 720,000) / 1,200,000 = 40%. The source reports 45%; the mismatch is flagged.

4
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
03 / TRACEABLE SOURCES
Clicking a reference opens the exact source passage and the full document. Finance inputs remain traceable to their original lines.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:49,000
04 / CODE-BASED ANALYSIS
Revenue growth is 20% from Q2 to Q3. The server shows both source inputs and the formula; the model does not perform the arithmetic.

6
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:57,000
05 / HR POLICY RETRIEVAL
The request routes to HR / Management. The annual leave entitlement is quoted from the employee handbook: 24 working days per year.

7
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:08,000
06 / CONFLICTING INFORMATION
The handbook allows 2 remote days; an addendum says 3. Both sources are shown. The system asks HR to confirm precedence.

8
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:16,000
07 / MISSING EVIDENCE
There is no parental leave policy in the accessible library. The assistant says it cannot find sufficient evidence and returns no invented source.

9
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:24,000
08 / UPLOAD A NEW REPORT
An Administrator uploads a synthetic Q4 PDF, selects Finance and assigns Shared access. PDF, Word and text uploads are supported.

10
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:34,000
09 / WORKING DATABASE AUTOMATION
The upload triggers extraction and an extractive summary. SQLite records a completed job, summary and processing attempt count.

11
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:43,000
10 / THE COMPLETE WORKFLOW
The newly uploaded PDF is immediately usable: Q4 gross margin is 46%, with citations to page 1 and the exact source metric lines.

12
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:51,000
11 / WORD DOCUMENT SUPPORT
A Word policy upload is indexed and summarized. The HR advisor retrieves the AED 2,000 training budget with its source reference.

13
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:58,000
12 / AUTHORIZED CONFIDENTIAL ACCESS
Administrator can retrieve the synthetic executive salary. This document is explicitly classified as confidential.

14
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:08,000
13 / STANDARD USER IS DENIED
After signing out and switching accounts, the same executive salary question has insufficient evidence. No confidential citation is returned.

15
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:16,000
14 / DIRECT ACCESS IS DENIED TOO
The exact source URL used by the Administrator returns Document not found for Standard User. Authorization is enforced by the server.

16
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:24,000
15 / FILTERED LIBRARY AND SUMMARIES
Standard User sees seven shared documents after the two uploads. The confidential source and its summary are absent.

17
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:32,000
16 / GENERAL KNOWLEDGE
The knowledge assistant retrieves the company services directly from the accessible overview document, with an inspectable source.

18
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:44,000
17 / ARCHITECTURE AND DEPLOYMENT
One local service and SQLite. Access is filtered before retrieval. Deploy behind HTTPS with secret management, monitoring and isolated parsing workers.

19
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:57,000
18 / RELIABILITY AND LIMITS
Tested: access denial, missing/conflicting evidence, incorrect financial inputs, rounding and zero denominators. Tested: corrupt uploads, durable job failure and retry, provider timeout / 401 / 429 / 503, invalid citations, and database failure. Limits: lexical retrieval, labelled policy conflicts, single-process automation, and strict financial report formats. Live model connectivity and Docker deployment remain unverified. See README.md, TEST_RESULTS.md and DISCLOSURE.md.

